  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "HSqc5H8eZJNjarL9VIP-z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 742.6644463656235,
      "y": 73.18001271722193,
      "width": 709.3511824996663,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1106172592,
      "version": 7805,
      "versionNonce": 789368301,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766590174812,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Questions to Ask\n- what time frame are we talking about. top k vidoes of all time? => this\nwould be simple because not much change here. conclusion: top k videos\nin past 1 hour, 1 day, 1 month and all time\n\n- next we talk about the window. is it sliding window or tumbling window.\nsliding window: If our current time is 10:06, the last 1 hour is the time\nbetween 9:06 and 10:06. Tumbling window: If our current time is 10:06,\nthe last 1 hour is the time between 9:00 and 10:00. conclusion: we solve\nfor tumbling window as they are easier to solve for.\n\n- next we put constraints on the size of k. In any system where your\nresult set might grow unbounded, having practical limits on your clients\nis a good idea. For almost all applications of top-K, 1k is a reasonable\nlimit.\n\n\n2) Functional Requirements:  \n- top k videos of all times \n- top k videos of tumbling window 1 {hour, day, month}\n\n------ out of scope --------- \n- arbitrary time windows \n- custom time period",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Questions to Ask\n- what time frame are we talking about. top k vidoes of all time? => this would be simple because not much change here. conclusion: top k videos in past 1 hour, 1 day, 1 month and all time\n\n- next we talk about the window. is it sliding window or tumbling window. sliding window: If our current time is 10:06, the last 1 hour is the time between 9:06 and 10:06. Tumbling window: If our current time is 10:06, the last 1 hour is the time between 9:00 and 10:00. conclusion: we solve for tumbling window as they are easier to solve for.\n\n- next we put constraints on the size of k. In any system where your result set might grow unbounded, having practical limits on your clients is a good idea. For almost all applications of top-K, 1k is a reasonable limit.\n\n\n2) Functional Requirements:  \n- top k videos of all times \n- top k videos of tumbling window 1 {hour, day, month}\n\n------ out of scope --------- \n- arbitrary time windows \n- custom time period",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b3QeLqnLHsxkexeN17H12",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1546.4482965020193,
