    {
      "id": "Y3jegDnt_wNByJWdgpEyA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1541.9962847457957,
      "y": 872.9203351513554,
      "width": 770.9084738017215,
      "height": 354.78692039128936,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 526339248,
      "version": 9499,
      "versionNonce": 939449891,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766590274226,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) One thing that needs to be acknowledged in our High level design is that\nwe have created index based on the view however from our kafka stream we\nwill have frequent updates to the view count hence frequent changes for the\nindex. Right now every view leads to 1 row in the table. 2) CMS: Count - min\nSketch How it works: say we have a videoId. CMS provides two methods -\nadd: uses a set of (n)hash functions increment value at n locaitons. -\nestimate: using those same hash functions goes to those n locations and\nreturns the minimum value from those n places.\n\nSolution: For each window we maintain a list of k min heap/ sorted set that\ncontaintain the top k videos. a new video view comes in we use CMS to add\nand estimate. If the estimated value is larger than the minimum value from\nthe heap or sorted set we remove it and add the new value else we do\nnothing.",
      "fontSize": 20.273538308073675,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) One thing that needs to be acknowledged in our High level design is that we have created index based on the view however from our kafka stream we will have frequent updates to the view count hence frequent changes for the index. Right now every view leads to 1 row in the table. 2) CMS: Count - min Sketch How it works: say we have a videoId. CMS provides two methods - add: uses a set of (n)hash functions increment value at n locaitons. - estimate: using those same hash functions goes to those n locations and returns the minimum value from those n places.\n\nSolution: For each window we maintain a list of k min heap/ sorted set that containtain the top k videos. a new video view comes in we use CMS to add and estimate. If the estimated value is larger than the minimum value from the heap or sorted set we remove it and add the new value else we do nothing.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
